About the name
--------------

This project is named in homage to Alan Lomax (1915-2002), the American
ethnomusicologist whose lifelong fieldwork building the Library of
Congress Archive of American Folk Song is, in spirit, what this
software tries to be in code: a careful, durable system for finding,
organising, and preserving a music collection.

lomax is an independent project. It is not produced by, endorsed by,
or otherwise affiliated with:

  - the Alan Lomax estate,
  - the Association for Cultural Equity (the nonprofit Alan Lomax
    founded in 1983 to repatriate his recordings to their communities
    of origin; https://www.culturalequity.org/), or
  - the Library of Congress American Folklife Center, which holds the
    Alan Lomax Collection.

For Alan Lomax's actual archive and recordings, please refer to the
Association for Cultural Equity at https://research.culturalequity.org/.

If at any point the Lomax estate, the Association for Cultural Equity,
or the Library of Congress objects to the use of this name, the
project commits in good faith to renaming. See docs/attribution.md
for the longer attribution statement (to be added in M0).
